{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations","id":1047834,"title":"Yantra limitations.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-12T12:57:48-08:00","id":1047834,"title":"Yantra limitations.","content":"Are we really limited to the Yantras/Path/Order Tools in the rulebook? I always assumed ever since the Open Dev introduced Yantras that they could be literally anything relevant to the theme or symbolism of the spell/path/order/casting style. I thought the ones in the rulebook were examples. Now I only find out that you really are just limited to the ones in the book. It feels so limiting to need merits and legacies just to increase your yantra selection. I don't think the yantras in the book are sufficient at all to build a style of casting or &quot;paradigm&quot; as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:19:07-08:00","id":1047843,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, the path and order tools are the yantras that are limited in scope. A yantra can be anything, from a book on a wall to a strange hat someone's wearing or a song in the air. Your dedicated tool is more specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:28:22-08:00","id":1047850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047843#post1047843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, the path and order tools are the yantras that are limited in scope. A yantra can be anything, from a book on a wall to a strange hat someone's wearing or a song in the air. Your dedicated tool is more specific.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, a Yantra cannot be anything.<br /> <br /> This has been discussed many times.<br /> <br /> In fact, Dave answered this question again just a few days ago.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#51651914\" target=\"_blank\">http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#51651914</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#117743\"><b>DaveB</b></span> <span style=\"color:#117743\">!!kn3vuELOelB</span> Thu 09 Feb 2017 18:49:52 <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#51651914\" target=\"_blank\">No.</a><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#q51651914\" target=\"_blank\">51651914</a> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/report/51651914/\" target=\"_blank\">Report</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#888888\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Quoted By: <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#51651947\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;51651947</a> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#51652080\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;51652080</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#789922\"><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/51634639/#51651649\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;51651649</a></span><br /> <br /> A Yantra has to be both appropriate to the spell and covered by something giving you the ability to use it as a Yantra. It's why your Dedicated Tool is not always usable for dice bonus, why Legacies and Merits give additional sources of Yantras, etc.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:30:31-08:00","id":1047854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Dawn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations#post1047834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the yantras in the book are sufficient at all to build a style of casting or &quot;paradigm&quot; as you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're more open than they look. What were you hoping to use as a yantra that seems like it isn't covered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:34:51-08:00","id":1047858,"title":"","content":"Sure.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, One Dawn, the path and order tools are the yantras that are limited in scope. A yantra can be almost anything, from a book on a wall to a strange hat someone's wearing or a song in the air. Your dedicated tool is more specific, and might not be appropriate for the spell being cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:38:46-08:00","id":1047862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047858#post1047858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, One Dawn, the path and order tools are the yantras that are limited in scope. A yantra can be almost anything, from a book on a wall to a strange hat someone's wearing or a song in the air. Your dedicated tool is more specific, and might not be appropriate for the spell being cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You are limited to the Yantras delineated in the Yantra list (p119-121). If you want more potential Yantras, tools or otherwise, you need to join a Legacy or purchase an appropriate merit like Shadow Name or Techne.<br /> <br /> Yantras are most certainly not open-ended. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:27:29-08:00","id":1047887,"title":"","content":"Not like it matters. There is no point sticking to +1 Yantras while almost any Mage can easily fill out their Yantra slots with bigger, better ones that are less flavorful, but much stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:39:40-08:00","id":1047895,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that it's not <i>just</i> Path/Order/Legacy tools that you're limited to; it's also environmental yantras, sympathy yantras, sacramental yantras... Carving a little humanoid figure and then burning it as a part of a ritual casting would make an appropriate sacrament, for example.<br /> <br /> Environment, sympathy, and sacrament all add a <i>lot</i> of potential and fuel for your spells, and help explain why Mages actively seek out and defend such things. Otherwise, you could use any old thing as a yantra and none would be particularly special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:40:18-08:00","id":1047896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047887#post1047887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not like it matters. There is no point sticking to +1 Yantras while almost any Mage can easily fill out their Yantra slots with bigger, better ones that are less flavorful, but much stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Other than Rote Mundras, there aren't a lot of +2 or greater Yantras that don't have inherent limitations or are only available because of a purchased merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:42:17-08:00","id":1047898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047887#post1047887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not like it matters. There is no point sticking to +1 Yantras while almost any Mage can easily fill out their Yantra slots with bigger, better ones that are less flavorful, but much stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>It matters at higher levels of gnosis when you have more slots than 2+ yantras. <br /> In my game, for non-combat spells, players went with mudra plus high speech. For combat spells, they went with either rote mudras or +1 dedicated tools that had been blessed with prime spells granting 8 or 9 again. Once they progress beyond low levels of gnosis, they'll start trying to incorporate more and more kinds of yantras so those +1 yantras can stack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:51:02-08:00","id":1047902,"title":"","content":"I would also note that many Yantras, including those provided by Shadow Name, have to be semiotically linked to the particular spell, and thus aren't usable with every spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:04:39-08:00","id":1047913,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to add that this topic is raised so often that it hopefully will be emphasized in the upcoming Mage FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:23:53-08:00","id":1047921,"title":"","content":"As I said, the one's in the book are severely limiting for my tastes. It's not enough if something symbolicaly and thematically appropriate to the Spell and Path, if its not in the Coin/Cup/Mirror/Rod/Weapon then they are not good. A lot of my draw in Mage is interpreting the symbolisms of things and how to use them. So basically player can't make any case on what is symbolic based on their praxis.<br /> <br /> This revalation killed half my character concepts, forcing me to get a Legacy or the Shadow Name merit to make them viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12979,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","user":"One Dawn","date":". 02-12-2017, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:24:12-08:00","id":1047922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047862#post1047862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. You are limited to the Yantras delineated in the Yantra list (p119-121). If you want more potential Yantras, tools or otherwise, you need to join a Legacy or purchase an appropriate merit like Shadow Name or Techne.<br /> <br /> Yantras are most certainly not open-ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>That list encompasses pretty much everything. Semiotics is the symbolism of things. A song can fittingly symbolize the spell you're going to cast with Sacred Geometry. Environment encompasses places and times. Between all that you have places, things, actions, times. What are you suggesting isn't capable of being a yantra?<br /> <br /> Everything that exists can't be an 'open ended' yantra, but everything can be a yantra because there's nothing that doesn't share some symbolism or meaning. It simply depends on the spell.<br /> <br /> If you want to narrow One Dawn's argument down to a specific spell, sure, but as they haven't been complaining about yantras not working with a specific spell, talking about spells in general makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2017, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:31:59-08:00","id":1047930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047922#post1047922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That list encompasses pretty much everything. Semiotics is the symbolism of things. A song can fittingly symbolize the spell you're going to cast with Sacred Geometry. Environment encompasses places and times. Between all that you have places, things, actions, times. What are you suggesting isn't capable of being a yantra?<br /> <br /> Everything that exists can't be an 'open ended' yantra, but everything can be a yantra because there's nothing that doesn't share some symbolism or meaning. It simply depends on the spell.<br /> <br /> If you want to narrow One Dawn's argument down to a specific spell, sure, but as they haven't been complaining about yantras not working with a specific spell, talking about spells in general makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no idea how you're interpreting Yantras like environment to encompass almost anything, particularly when merits like Shadow Name or Techne, no less Legacies, are specifically designed to expand the range of Yantras.<br /> <br /> The explicit rules and DaveB make it quite clear that it takes a lot more than something being allegedly symbolic of Path and spell to qualify as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:38:18-08:00","id":1047937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047930#post1047930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how you're interpreting Yantras like environment to encompass almost anything, particularly when merits like Shadow Name or Techne, no less Legacies, are specifically designed to expand the range of Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea how you aren't. There's no environment that can't be symbolic of something. The book itself says it, and Dave said it, 'Places and times in the Fallen World can bring about the Supernal if they reflect the spell a mage is using.' Providing the spell has some symbolism with the environment, like freeing a ghoul from blood bondage during the Fourth of July, or calming an enraged monster in a serene glade, it works as a yantra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The explicit rules and DaveB make it quite clear that it takes a lot more than something being allegedly symbolic of Path and spell to qualify as a Yantra. </div> </div> </div>No, he said that's what it takes. You posted the quote yourself. It must be representative of the spell, and be something the mage can use. Anyone can use an environmental yantra.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:40:19-08:00","id":1047940,"title":"","content":"I love Mage because I love semiotics, and love to find the meaning of something even if it's small and insgnificant. I love how these meaning and symbols are used to fuel and tap into the Supernal to make symbol reality. This revalation I had about the limits of Yantras broke immersion for me. Suddenly the symbols were no longer subjective, critical endeavor. Appaently somethings hold no symbolic meaning after all. There is an objective Truth in a game about making your Will bend reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:42:11-08:00","id":1047943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047937#post1047937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea how you aren't. There's no environment that can't be symbolic of something. The book itself says it, and Dave said it, 'Places and times in the Fallen World can bring about the Supernal if they reflect the spell a mage is using.' Providing the spell has some symbolism with the environment, like freeing a ghoul from blood bondage during the Fourth of July, or calming an enraged monster in a serene glade, it works as a yantra.<br /> <br /> No, he said that's what it takes. You posted the quote yourself. It must be representative of the spell, and be something the mage can use. Anyone can use an environmental yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Environment Yantra only allows a bonus if the spell is cast at a specific location and is semiotically-linked to the spell itself, no more, no less.<br /> <br /> It's not a catch-all for anything symbolically linked to a spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Environment<br /> Places and times in the Fallen World can bring about the<br /> Supernal if they reflect the spell a mage is using. An Acanthus<br /> may use the sun at noon to see through falsehoods, while a<br /> Mastigos might use the light of the full moon reflected in a<br /> pool of water to scry across vast distances. Location is just as<br /> important \u2014 many Obrimos seek out churches to perform spells<br /> of persuasion, command, and stewardship. Some wizards prepare ritual spaces that contain multiple Yantras \u2014 combining a<br /> favorable environment with Atlantean runes and magical tools<br /> into a summoning circle. Such a location combines three Yantras in one place \u2014 but inexperienced mystics must take their<br /> time, and a mage\u2019s enemies will soon learn where best to strike.<br /> An environment has to link to the spell itself, not just the<br /> mage. The Obrimos in a church cannot use it as a Yantra to magically charge her cellphone. The magic must link to what Sleepers<br /> know about a place or time, not because their perceptions cause<br /> Supernal notice but because their actions unconsciously reflect<br /> the Supernal attributes of a place.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: Casting in an appropriate location grants a 1-die bonus.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:22:25-08:00","id":1047977,"title":"","content":"Well, not the first tine I disagreed with things Dave said what the game should be. I'll continue running Yantras the way I see fit, which I feel is more thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:22:48-08:00","id":1047978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Dawn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047940#post1047940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appaently somethings hold no symbolic meaning after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, some things <i>require investment to make a meaningful difference to your magical praxis.</i> This is what Orders and Legacies and Shadow Names and Dedicated Tools are for. This is why sympathy and sacraments and environments are so broad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is an objective Truth in a game about making your Will bend reality. </div> </div> </div>This has been the case the entire time. Awakening is not Ascension \u2014 you're not making up potent mystical associations wholesale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T20:34:04-08:00","id":1048051,"title":"","content":"I interpreted the book very much as nofather did.<br /> For me its all about the specifics, with the vague guideline if it looks like it would help the spell it's a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Casting lightning from on high; environmental yantra<br /> growing gills while eating fish; symbolic yantra<br /> summoning the ghost while holding their skull; symbolic yantra<br /> freeing some ones mind who's high on LSD; Symbolic yantra<br /> granting your self echolocation while deep with in a bat infested cave; environmental <br /> turning invisible while wrapping your self in a cloak; symbolic tool <br /> <br /> something like summoning an old testament wrath of god spell? Try Egypt environmental yantra via historical context with the sleeper world. (a very Paternoster thought.)<br /> <br /> I'm even more than willing to give rather large yantra bonuses as mechanical incentive for clever ideas. <br /> <br /> But Bradford why the rather intense defense of restricting yantras? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T20:50:05-08:00","id":1048054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047937#post1047937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how you aren't. There's no environment that can't be symbolic of something.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Every place in this part of reality counts as an Environment Yantra&quot; is a specific quality of the Temenos based on the pure density of symbolism at work \u2014 much like how a spirit with Time as an Influence doesn't have the Resonant Condition for anything and everything in normal material reality just based on the fact that time is passing for that object, creature, or location, not every place contains elements whose symbolism is accessible to Sleepers.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the breadth of Instruments mages can leverage, but let's not confuse matters by according all places equal significance when the entire point of Yantras being able to provide a bonus is that they <i>are </i>significant things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T20:54:11-08:00","id":1048055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048051#post1048051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Bradford why the rather intense defense of restricting yantras?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's how the rules are actually written, the list is exhaustive. Environmental Yantras for instance can seem to be a little more flexible, but it isn't dependent on what the Mage thinks is symbolic, it's dependent on the symbolism that Sleepers associate with the environment. Casting a lightning bolt from just any old high place isn't going to work, it has to be from a high place that Sleepers associate with lightning. The &quot;flexibility&quot; you're looking for is better expressed by using the Merits that expand Yantra options or borrowing from the Yantra options provided by your Order or Legacy. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:13:05-08:00","id":1048057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048055#post1048055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because that's how the rules are actually written, the list is exhaustive. Environmental Yantras for instance can seem to be a little more flexible, but it isn't dependent on what the Mage thinks is symbolic, it's dependent on the symbolism that Sleepers associate with the environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat cause I'm the ST and I make that decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048055#post1048055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting a lightning bolt from just any old high place isn't going to work,</div> </div> </div> </div>I said on high which is the symbolic turn of phrase your character would need to turn any high place into symbolic resonance for passing judgment and hurling divine fury. very fitting for Obrimos. but in a sense your right this is a game of degrees +1 through +5. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048055#post1048055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;flexibility&quot; you're looking for is better expressed by using the Merits that expand Yantra options or borrowing from the Yantra options provided by your Order or Legacy. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not looking for flexibility, but yes those are there as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:20:47-08:00","id":1048059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048057#post1048057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat cause I'm the ST and I make that decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we're talking about houserules, this conversation has lost its common ground at this exact juncture and is no longer productive for the general user of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:22:04-08:00","id":1048060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048055#post1048055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;flexibility&quot; you're looking for is better expressed by using the Merits that expand Yantra options or borrowing from the Yantra options provided by your Order or Legacy. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, this is one of the many reasons why Shadow Name is so appealing: you get to build in symbolism that plays to your intended areas of specialty instead of relying on chance and preparation, with the downside being if you want to venture outside of those specialties you have to either assemble materials the long way or go through the extensive process of rebuilding your magical identity.<br /> <br /> I'll freely cop that my reading of how Dedicating Tools works is not explicit and primarily based on extrapolating from the fact that it's a universal ability whose effects are also part of a universal ability whose only limitation is Size (and the fact that we don't strictly know how Order Tool categories form unless that's instead a function of the Sects' generalized equivalent of &quot;the [Latin for 'X of the Dragon'] terms are the Diamond Orders' institutional Shadow Names built to evoke Atlantean society&quot;), but even that conclusion is drawn under the assumption that potent bonuses are increasingly limited \u2014 you only get <i>one Dedicated Tool at a time</i>, soul stones notwithstanding, and the unambiguously strongest single Yantra bonuses are 1) bound to individual spells and dependent upon other stats, 2) bound to the symbolism of a defined magical actor thematically related to other defined magical actors, and 3) attached to items acquired from beyond the material realm with significant effort and consumed as part of the spell. [Honorable mention goes to 4) a chunk of your mystical superiors' magical insight, crystalized into an object.]<br /> <br /> This tends to incentivize certain activities, even if in practice the bonuses only offset enough penalties to give you a &quot;free&quot; spell factor or two, and for the sake of ludonarrative cohesion you're going to want that degree of extra power to be owed to something perceptible enough that it evokes the kind of Stories About Enlightened Magicians that serve as part of the basis for the template's image within the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:27:01-08:00","id":1048062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048059#post1048059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we're talking about houserules, this conversation has lost its common ground at this exact juncture and is no longer productive for the general user of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure (although their is an ST in every game), but my question to Bradford although if you Mrmdubois or anyone else for that matter have a thought on why you would want yantra to be limited?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:34:58-08:00","id":1048063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048062#post1048062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure (although their is an ST in every game), but my question to Bradford although if you Mrmdubois or anyone else for that matter have a thought on why you would want yantra to be limited?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the game is clearly not written from the assumption that <i>literally everything </i>is suitable as a Yantra (take note that Active Prime Sight wouldn't have seen fit to mention detecting viable Yantras if it was) and because limitations make the game meaningfully distinct in a way that you don't get from raw declaratives being able to get leverage on the Fallen World through potentially extremely tenuous connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:41:23-08:00","id":1048065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048062#post1048062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure (although their is an ST in every game), but my question to Bradford although if you Mrmdubois or anyone else for that matter have a thought on why you would want yantra to be limited?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, by the way their name is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar618_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"618\" data-vbnamecard=\"618\">branford</a> not Bradford. Getting even the simple (and polite) things wrong doesn't help your position any.<br /> <br /> The fact that there's an ST present in every game doesn't in any way detract from the point that the game is written in a certain way. An ST has the prerogative to change things to suit their game, but at the point at which they do they can't claim to be making an argument that has a basis in the material provided in the rules. They have crossed the bounds of the common material provided to all players and STs into a more personal realm. There's nothing wrong with that, but it adds nothing to understanding where the game is coming from in the general sense that the devs have provided from their work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-13-2017, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:55:54-08:00","id":1048066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048063#post1048063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the game is clearly not written from the assumption that <i>literally everything </i>is suitable as a Yantra</div> </div> </div> </div>suddenly i feel like your conflating any with every. but why? Why would you rather have it this way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048063#post1048063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(take note that Active Prime Sight wouldn't have seen fit to mention detecting viable Yantras if it was) and because limitations make the game meaningfully distinct in a way that you don't get from raw declaratives being able to get leverage on the Fallen World through potentially extremely tenuous connections.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Prime can identify yantras for specific spells, or specific hypothetical spells and and of course yantras that are in use or have been used.<br /> in practice its either a creativity primer from the ST or a investigative tool.<br /> The more tenuous the connection weaker the bonus if one should be given at all. It does have to make sense after all. that being said symbolism is subjective and ultimately comes down to an out of game decision made by the ST and agreed upon by the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T22:11:42-08:00","id":1048068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048062#post1048062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure (although their is an ST in every game), but my question to Bradford although if you Mrmdubois or anyone else for that matter have a thought on why you would want yantra to be limited?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It not a matter of whether I want Yantras to be limited, but rather that the actual rules clearly both limit the type, scope, nature and use of Yantras and detail how a mage may expand their repertoire of potential Yantras with merits and legacies (and I expect more rules in Signs of Sorcery).<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I believe that the listed Yantras are indeed sufficiently broad to still be meaningful and thematic, and that the effective free-form Yantra rules as suggested by some would be problematic. Mage abilities are already sufficiently broad and powerful enough without the need to permit virtually anything to provide even more bonuses. It also eliminates potential arguments or delays at the game table in that there's no need to discuss how every rock or paperweight is relevant to every spell. Lastly, limiting Yantras makes matters like legacies and purchasing and using the shadow name and similar merits all the more important, something that was definitely a design decision in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 02-13-2017, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T22:19:41-08:00","id":1048069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048066#post1048066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">suddenly i feel like your conflating any with every.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You can use every object for this&quot; and &quot;You can use any object for this&quot; have identical meanings in a context where a limited number of discrete things can be used at once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but why? Why would you rather have it this way. </div> </div> </div>Because I prefer my mages to seek out magical real estate and items of symbolic potency and fight for scraps of lore like the game describes them doing when I attempt to develop an understanding of how the game and its world work instead of tossing together misreading-based absurdities. There are substantially broad categories of Chain \u2014 these demonstrably do not propagate that quality to the whole of Awakened mnemonics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prime can identify yantras for specific spells, or specific hypothetical spells and and of course yantras that are in use or have been used. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Anything the mage can use as a Yantra.&quot; No additional qualifiers on that descriptor.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in practice its either a creativity primer from the ST or a investigative tool. </div> </div> </div>The Sight does not tell you the symbolism of an object \u2014 you have to know it to use it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The more tenuous the connection weaker the bonus if one should be given at all. </div> </div> </div>There is no smaller bonus than one die, the number of things that provide a bonus greater than two dice can be counted on one hand, and the entire complaint at work in this thread is that not all levels of symbolism offer a Yantra bonus. The only benefit a +0 Yantra offers is both specific to Sympathy Yantras and a non-benefit outside of that context.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tenuous connections don't provide a bonus at all&quot; is a pretty direct acknowledgement that not everything is viable as an Instrument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T22:27:21-08:00","id":1048070,"title":"","content":"For those who want more of a free-form feel to their Yantras, I would suggest focusing on Sacraments when spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Although limited as one use items, they can be almost anything and provide a range of potential bonuses based on the strength of the semiotic connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T22:45:02-08:00","id":1048072,"title":"","content":"Okay, folks. Here is an exhaustive list of everything that can be used as a Yantra, paraphrased from the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Places:</b><ul><li>A Demesne that is semiotically linked to the spell (+2)</li> <li><i>Any environment </i>that is semiotically linked to the spell (+1)</li> <li>A supernal verge that is semiotically linked to the spell (+2)</li> </ul><b>Actions:</b><ul><li>Concentrating on the spell (+2 to a spell with Duration &gt; 1 turn, but the spell ends early if the mage takes any damage or a non-reflexive action during the spell\u2019s duration)</li> <li>Intoning the spell in High Speech (+2 dice, requires High Speech Merit, cannot be used reflexively)</li> <li>The Skill associated with a Rote, also known as a Mudra (+ [Mage\u2019s dots in the associated Skill], to a maximum of +5. Only usable with Rotes.)</li> <li>Writing the spell in High Speech (+2 dice, requires High Speech Merit, the spell ends if the rune is disrupted or damaged)</li> </ul><b>Tools:</b><ul><li>A coin, cup, mirror, rod, or wand made of a Path-appropriate material that is semiotically linked to the spell (+1)<ul><li>Appropriate materials for Acanthus include glass, crystal, silver, rapiers, bows, <i>any \u201cprecise\u201d weapon</i>, and <i>anything reflective</i></li> <li>Appropriate materials for Mastigos include iron, brass, leather, curved swords, whips, <i>any \u201ccruel\u201d weapon</i>, and <i>anything that has been worked</i></li> <li>Appropriate materials for Moros include lead, bone, gems, hammers, maces, <i>any crushing weapon</i>, and <i>anything that has been buried</i></li> <li>Appropriate materials for Obrimos include steel, petrified wood, gold, double-edged swords, spears, <i>any \u201cnoble\u201d weapon</i>, and <i>anything that has been \u201cperfected\u201d</i></li> <li>Appropriate materials for Thyrsus include wood, copper, stone, slings, <i>any \u201chunting\u201d weapon</i> and <i>anything natural</i></li> </ul></li> <li>Any Order-appropriate object that is semiotically linked to the spell (+1)<ul><li>Appropriate objects for Adimantine Arrows include <i>any martial tool</i></li> <li>Appropriate objects for Guardians of the Veil include cloaks, masks, and veils</li> <li>Appropriate objects for Mystigogues include books, <i>any writing</i>, and <i>any language</i></li> <li>Appropriate objects for Silver Ladder members include <i>any sign of authority</i></li> <li>Appropriate objects for Seers of the Throne include <i>any one symbol or word</i></li> <li>Appropriate objects for Libertines include <i>any \u201ccomplex\u201d mechanism or system</i>, as well as <i>any practice from Sleeper culture</i> that the Libertine has the Techne Merit for</li> </ul></li> <li>The symbol of an Exarch that is semiotically linked to the spell (+ [Mage\u2019s dots in the Prelacy Merit], requires Prelacy \u009f\u009f\u009f\u009f \u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">+)</span></span></span></li> <li><i>Any object that represents the subject of the spell</i> (Bonus varies based on the object\u2019s Sympathy with the subject - +2 for a representation of the subject as they are in the present, +1 for a representation of the subject in the past, +0 for an indirect representation of the subject. Required to cast spells on the subject with the Sympathetic Range and/or Temporal Sympathy Attainment(s))</li> <li><i>Any object </i>that is semiotically linked to the spell (Bonus varies based on the difficulty of obtaining the object - +1 for most objects, +2 if the object requires significant effort to obtain, +3 if the object comes from somewhere other than the material realm. The object must be destroyed in the process of casting the spell.)</li> <li>A Shadow Name that is semiotically linked to the spell (+ [Mage\u2019s dots in the Shadow Name Merit], +1 If the Mage\u2019s Cabal all have an appropriate Cabal Theme Merit {stacks with Shadow Name})</li> <li>Spending Mana from a Leyline with resonance that is semiotically linked to the spell (+1)</li> <li>The Mage\u2019s Dedicated Tool (-2 Paradox dice. Can also be used as a Path or Order Tool if it is semiotically linked with the spell)</li> </ul><b>Legacy:</b><ul><li>A place, object, or action that is specifically used as a Yantra by the Mage's Legacy and semiotically associated with the spell (Bonus varies, +1 for most places, objects, and actions, +2 for places, objects, and actions that impose negative Conditions or require rare materials, extra time, or special care. Usually can't be performed reflexively.)</li> </ul>So, are Yantras limited to the things listed in the book? Yes. Can practically anything be used as a Yantra as long as it is semiotically linked to the spell? Yes. That list includes a fucking lot of shit. The thing that I think gets people mixed up is Path and Order Tools, which are significantly more limited than most other forms of Yantra. But just because a thing can\u2019t be used as a Path or Order tool doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t be used as a Yantra. You're really more restricted in <i>what type</i> of Yantra a particular place, action, or object can be used as (and by extension what bonus it can provide) than by whether or not it can be used as a Yantra at all.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tagging <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12979\" data-vbnamecard=\"12979\">One Dawn</a> in, because I think they would want to see this and I worry they might have come to the conclusion that Yantras are less flexible than they are and abandoned the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-13-2017, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T22:53:26-08:00","id":1048073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048072#post1048072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, folks. Here is an extensive list of everything that can be used as a Yantra, paraphrased from the book.<br /> <br /> So, are Yantras limited to the things listed in the book? Yes. <b>Can practically anything be used as a Yantra as long as it is semiotically linked to the spell? Yes</b>. That list includes a fucking lot of shit. The thing that I think gets people is Path and Order Tools, which are significantly more limited than most other forms of Yantra. But just because a thing can\u2019t be used as a Path or Order tool doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t be used as a Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, practically anything <b>cannot</b> be used as a Yantra just because it might be semiotically linked to the spell, other than some very specific and limited places, shadow names or one-use sacraments.<br /> <br /> Between Order and Path tools, mundras, High Speech, etc., mages have ample Yantra choices, further expanded by merits and legacies, but Yantras are hardly even close to as open-ended as some suggest.<br /> <br /> Edit: However, that was a very handy Yantra reference list. I would just recommend adding the Techne merit and a note about Legacy yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 02-13-2017, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:07:18-08:00","id":1048075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048073#post1048073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, practically anything <b>cannot</b> be used as a Yantra just because it might be semiotically linked to the spell, other than some very specific and limited places, shadow names or one-use sacraments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, practically anything can be used as a Yantra as long as it is semiotically linked to the spell. You might just have to actually be there or to destroy the object. Refute me if you can. Name one place, action, or object that can't be used as a Yantra (including an Environment Yantra, Mudra, or Sacrament Yantra) for any spell at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048073#post1048073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between Order and Path tools, mundras, High Speech, etc., mages have ample Yantra choices, further expanded by merits and legacies, but Yantras are hardly even close to as open-ended as some suggest.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Path and Order Tools</i> are hardly even close to as open-ended as some suggest. But Path and Order Tools are not the only form of Yantra. Sacraments are a from of Yantra and they include any object that is semiotically linked to the spell, as long as you destroy it. Environments are a form of Yantra and they include any place that is semiotically linked to the spell, as long as you are there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048073#post1048073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: However, that was a very handy Yantra reference list. I would just recommend adding the Techne merit and a note about Legacy yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Techne is in there under the things that count as appropriate objects for Libertines to use as Order Tools. Good point about Legacy Yantras, though. I'll edit it into the post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-13-2017, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:15:50-08:00","id":1048077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048073#post1048073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, practically anything <b>cannot</b> be used as a Yantra just because it might be semiotically linked to the spell, other than some very specific and limited places, shadow names or one-use sacraments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potential sympathies and sacraments make up a significant portion of the Phenomenal World and sacraments in particular serve as the primary means of actually using Praxis as a means of initiating into a Legacy without the right Path or Order.<br /> <br /> The problem is that people are misapplying the degree of universality relative to the degree of specificity when it comes to what you can use as a Yantra \u2014 I'd clarify that Prime Sight only works on recognizable symbolism; most potential Instruments of Sympathy aren't going to ping it for the simple reason that most mages don't know everyone around them and the things connected to them without effort, while prospective Sacraments are going to have their usability (and thus their visibility) constrained by lack of knowledge of their composition. (Environmental Yantras tend to have their availability enhanced by the basic Occult grounding the Orders facilitate.)<br /> <br /> Notably, this means most forms of identification still register to the Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:22:25-08:00","id":1048078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048075#post1048075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, practically anything can be used as a Yantra as long as it is semiotically linked to the spell. You might just have to actually be there or to destroy the object. Refute me if you can. Name one place, action, or object that can't be used as a Yantra (including an Environment or Sacrament Yantra) for any spell at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Path and Order Tools</i> are hardly even close to as open-ended as some suggest. But Path and Order Tools are not the only form of Yantra. Sacraments are a from of Yantra and they include any object that is semiotically linked to the spell, as long as you destroy it. Environments are a form of Yantra and they include any place that is semiotically linked to the spell, as long as you are there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Techne is in there under the things that count as appropriate objects for Libertines to use as Order Tools. Good point about Legacy Yantras, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'll note that in a prior post I suggested for those who want more open-ended Yantras to focus on using Sacraments.<br /> <br /> However, the discussion has largely concerned using virtually any object or action as a Yantra simply because it might be symbolically linked to the spell, without any inherent limitations, including those of Sacraments or even location/environment. For something or act to be used as a Yantra, it needs to be both semiotically appropriate and fall within one of the delineated Yantra categories (and limits). <br /> <br /> Our disagreement is not as large as it may seem, as I've always noted the rules already provide a significant degree of Yantra flexibility and adequate means to expand Yantra options even further. I object to those who suggest that even these relatively minor limits are still too constricting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:28:30-08:00","id":1048080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048078#post1048078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that in a prior post I suggested for those who want more open-ended Yantras to focus on using Sacraments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Sacraments are a form of Yantra, so by your own admission, practically anything can be used as a Yantra. Not anything can be used as <i>any type</i> of Yantra, but anything can be used as <i>some </i>type of Yantra. Again, you're more limited in <i>what </i>kind of Yantra a thing can be used as, not in <i>if</i> a thing can be used as a Yantra at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048078#post1048078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the discussion has largely concerned using virtually any object or action as a Yantra simply because it might be symbolically linked to the spell, without any inherent limitations, including those of Sacraments or even location/environment. For something or act to be used as a Yantra, it needs to be both semiotically appropriate and fall within one of the delineated Yantra categories (and limits).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read the thread, and I don't think the people who have been saying &quot;basically anything can be used as a Yantra&quot; are arguing that they can do so without any limitations. You might be arguing against a point no one is making.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048078#post1048078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our disagreement is not as large as it may seem, as I've always noted the rules already provide a significant degree of Yantra flexibility and adequate means to expand Yantra options even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is precisely what my post was intended to express.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048078#post1048078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I object to those who suggest that even these relatively minor limits are still too constricting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't think anyone is actually suggesting that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:33:56-08:00","id":1048082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048080#post1048080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I don't think anyone is actually suggesting that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some have clearly and unequivocally argued that all a Yantra, whether object, act, place, etc, should require is a semiotic link to the spell. That's it, nothing else, and any other qualifiers are not consistent with Mage's gnostic themes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:35:03-08:00","id":1048083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048082#post1048082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some have clearly and unequivocally argued that all a Yantra, whether object, act, place, etc, should require is a semiotic link to the spell. That's it, nothing else, and any other qualifiers are not consistent with Mage's gnostic themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you quote that, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:46:53-08:00","id":1048091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048083#post1048083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you quote that, please?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By way of example,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047921#post1047921\"> this</a>.<br /> <br /> However, this is also hardly the first time this precise issue has arisen on the OPP forums or elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:03:36-08:00","id":1048094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048091#post1048091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By way of example,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047921#post1047921\">this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I see there is a new user, who may or may not be new to Awakening 2e, who had just been told that you are limited to a specific set of options regarding what can be used as a Yantra (not what can be used as a Tool Yantra) and saying in response:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Dawn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1047921#post1047921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not enough if something symbolicaly and thematically appropriate to the Spell and Path, if its not in the Coin/Cup/Mirror/Rod/Weapon then they are not good.</div> </div> </div> </div>which is demonstrably untrue. This user may or may not have overestimated the flexibility of Yantras in general, there's not enough information in the post for me to tell, but they did come away from the exchange with a false conclusion. I would rather (correctly) inform them that yes, it <i>is</i> enough if something is symbolically and thematically appropriate to the spell, you just might have to break it if it's not a coin, cup, rod, mirror, or weapon, than to assume an unspoken &quot;with no further restrictions&quot; in his statement and try to correct that assumed assertion. You catch more flies with honey and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048091#post1048091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, this is also hardly the first time this precise issue has arisen on the OPP forums or elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and when those people show up, I will gladly join you in pointing out to them that some objects have to be sacrificed in order to be used as Yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-13-2017, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:09:46-08:00","id":1048098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048094#post1048094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I see there is a new user, who may or may not be new to Awakening 2e, who had just been told that you are limited to a specific set of options regarding what can be used as a Yantra (not what can be used as a Tool Yantra) saying, &quot;if its not in the Coin/Cup/Mirror/Rod/Weapon then they are not good.&quot;, which is demonstrably untrue. This user may or may not have overestimated the flexibility of Yantras in general, there's not enough information in the post for me to tell, but they did come away from the exchange with a false conclusion. I would rather (correctly) inform them that yes, anything with a Semiotic link to the spell <i>can</i> be used as a Yantra, you just might have to break it if it's not a coin, cup, rod, mirror, or weapon&quot; and work from common ground, than to correct an assumed implication of their statement. You catch more flies with honey and all that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, and when those people show up, I will gladly join you in pointing out to them that some objects have to be sacrificed in order to be used as Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The argument about using anything with a semiotic link is not limited to just objects, rather it also includes any &quot;environment&quot; (not just specific locations or times) and even actions or conduct like rituals, matters that cannot be sacrificed as Sacraments or would otherwise fall within the delineated Yantra categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:27:34-08:00","id":1048103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048098#post1048098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument about using anything with a semiotic link is not limited to just objects, rather it also includes any &quot;environment&quot; (not just specific locations or times) and even actions or conduct like rituals, matters that cannot be sacrificed as Sacraments or would otherwise fall within the delineated Yantra categories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If it's a place and therefore can't be used as a Sacrament, you've got to be there. If it's an action and therefore can't be used as a sacrament, you've got to use it as a Mudra. So, add &quot;be there, or tie it to a Rote&quot; after &quot;you might have to break it&quot;, and my point still stands. The better solution here would be to <i>expand</i> their understanding of Yantras, not to shut them down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:31:03-08:00","id":1048104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048072#post1048072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, folks. Here is an exhaustive list of everything that can be used as a Yantra, paraphrased from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed Soul Stones. Your own Soul Stone is +1 Dice -2 Paradox (basically, a Dedicated Tool), Soul Stone of someone else is +2, and Soul Stone of someone with bigger Gnosis than you is +3. Which makes a Cabal sharing their Soulstones for spellcasting incredibly potent, and probably another case of unintended gameplay pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:33:44-08:00","id":1048105,"title":"","content":"Thinking on Sacramental Yantras. It's like you've got to burn out the symbolic supernal truth from the fallen world object. Similar to using an incorrect fuse, and burning it out. You get your juice but the object needs to be replaced before you can do it again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:38:12-08:00","id":1048106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048104#post1048104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed Soul Stones. Your own Soul Stone is +1 Dice -2 Paradox (basically, a Dedicated Tool), Soul Stone of someone else is +2, and Soul Stone of someone with bigger Gnosis than you is +3. Which makes a Cabal sharing their Soulstones for spellcasting incredibly potent, and probably another case of unintended gameplay pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say unintended, but I read it as Social Plot. I can image some uncomfortable discussions with the masters about why their soul stones were found in compromising sanctums of the enemy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  spell 02-13-2017, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:44:14-08:00","id":1048109,"title":"","content":"I'm talking about player characters creating SoulStones and giving them to each other any time a spell is cast outside of combat. With your typical Cabal of 3-4 people, that's enough to fill all Yantra slots and some. And if you have a single member with Superior Gnosis, it's really tempting to make him create 2 or 3 and supercharge your spells. <br /> Which *CAN* invite interesting results and consequences - say, Consilium Enforcer being given a Soul Stone from each Council Master both as a token of authority AND an incredible power boost, or as a way to make younger Mages want to pledge themselves to wiser ones, hoping to get Favored Apprentice Status that comes with a prize of their Masters Soul Stone - but I don't think it was setting-intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:44:22-08:00","id":1048110,"title":"","content":"@Charlaquin<br /> Thanks for the clarification. I feel you are the only one here that was helpful in the discussion by providing those examples. Looks like I'll be sticking with sacraments and environemntal Yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:48:40-08:00","id":1048111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Dawn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048110#post1048110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin<br /> Thanks for the clarification. I feel you are the only one here that was helpful in the discussion by providing those examples. Looks like I'll be sticking with sacraments and environemntal Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pick a fitting Shadow Name and you can include actions too. Honestly, Shadow Name is so good that it feels like Merit Tax. It's also worth inventing your own Legacy; it's cheap and Legacy benefits are front loaded as hell. Biggest perks of Legacy aren't Legacy Attainments (they tend to universally suck), but 3rd Ruling Arcanum, another way to replenish Mana, and expanded range of Yantras. You can do this as fast as Gnosis 3 + 1 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T00:52:56-08:00","id":1048112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048106#post1048106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say unintended, but I read it as Social Plot. I can image some uncomfortable discussions with the masters about why their soul stones were found in compromising sanctums of the enemy</div> </div> </div> </div>WHW has a really bad habit of assuming everything's a mistake, and implying we're incompetent every other post.<br /> <br /> Yantras work as intended. No one is going to call you names for house ruling it. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:00:10-08:00","id":1048114,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> <br /> It may not be written as RAW setting assumption. but can you really take that approach when the dev have the stated goal being the books as a toolkit. In that Light I think it's a fantastic local setting element. The fact that soul stones are a wisdom ting would create a lot of debate over the issue. Add to that the cannibalization of your soul's potential, which no one can reasonable reach anyways(power stat 10). The question becomes a &quot;why not?&quot; with good points on both sides. There is lots of room to use soul stones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:08:50-08:00","id":1048119,"title":"","content":"It just sounds like you have to declare that your Yantra is more than just semiotically viable. Meaning, your ST makes the distinction or acknowledgment that your choice of Yantra applies to the given spell.<br /> <br /> The connection is made more valid when you cement it via Legacy.<br /> <br /> I'm with the <i>&quot;anything can be a Yantra for some thing&quot;</i> brigade.<br /> <br /> The semiotic razz-ma-tazz seems to just necessitate ST agreement that the idea of the (prospective) Yantra is symbolically recognized by more than just a small group of people.<br /> <br /> The thing people are trying to avoid is, as Satchel noted, wholesale inflation of symbolism via Tenemos. I believe the Order and Path tools are so specific because their platonic idea is so well cemented. When you equate &quot;high place&quot; to lightning, most people don't necessarily equate any high place to lightning. (Although, you could perhaps get more flexible if there is already a storm brewing or active.) You're basically stating &quot;height is a thing that is associated with lightning; ergo, any height will suffice&quot; or more arbitrary yet &quot;this is a building that is sufficiently tall to qualify as a metaphor for lightning; and then using anything defined as a building because a building is higher than the absence of a building ... (aka height acquired?)&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps if your story ingrained a historically recognized symbol of loud booms and flashes coming from the rooftops in a prominent war gone by? Something NPCs can vaguely, or distinctly, remember as a big deal. Or perhaps you have a Legacy of people that rain lightning down on others from on high; specifically a penchant for assassinating with a loud crack of thunder from rooftop to unsuspecting window (like old Church spires and mounted Gargoyles)? &quot;If the Thunder Boys are contracted to kill you, avoid all windows; they kinda revel in that shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the OP. Anything <b>can</b> be a Yantra for certain things, but it cannot be seen as a willy-nilly declaration of personal symbolism -- &quot;I think this bag is cute enough to be a hat.&quot; I think that's the whole reason for the Legacy method, is so you can weave it into the story to give it the necessary <i>significance</i>.<br /> <br /> I think the intent isn't to limit, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar618_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"618\" data-vbnamecard=\"618\">branford</a> have noted already, but instead I think the game wants you to invest more than passive intrigue in Yantra. It's supposed to be a strong tool.<br /> <br /> What use does an NPC (or you) have in targeting Yantra if replacing the sacred knife is as easy as whipping out your back-up existential plastic butter knife? Not to say you can't use that existential butter-knife, but you better get cracking on why that particular butter knife is so dang special, LOL.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To avoid breaking every session into a series of &quot;Here's why this is really symbolic&quot; debates, it is utterly necessary that these strong symbolisms are already acknowledged by your ST. Trying to whip out a whole previously never-discussed narrative over the importance of your existential butter knife <i>is extremely uncool.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 02-13-2017, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:16:47-08:00","id":1048120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Dawn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048110#post1048110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin<br /> Thanks for the clarification. I feel you are the only one here that was helpful in the discussion by providing those examples. Looks like I'll be sticking with sacraments and environemntal Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just note that Environmental Yantras only apply to specific, semiotically-linked physical locations and times. It's not as broad a circumstance as some imply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048111#post1048111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pick a fitting Shadow Name and you can include actions too. Honestly, Shadow Name is so good that it feels like Merit Tax. It's also worth inventing your own Legacy; it's cheap and Legacy benefits are front loaded as hell. Biggest perks of Legacy aren't Legacy Attainments (they tend to universally suck), but 3rd Ruling Arcanum, <b>another way to replenish Mana</b>, and expanded range of Yantras. You can do this as fast as Gnosis 3 + 1 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given all the expanded uses for mana and its similarly aggravated scarcity in 2e (no free mana at Hallows or recharging artifact mana batteries), the legacy ability to obtain mana using an oblation <i><b>without need for a Hallow</b></i> is as important as that potential third Ruling Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:16:47-08:00","id":1048121,"title":"","content":"DELETE - DUPLICATE<br /> <br /> EXARCHS AT WORK","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:22:59-08:00","id":1048123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048119#post1048119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing people are trying to avoid is, as Satchel noted, wholesale inflation of symbolism via Tenemos. <b>I believe the Order and Path tools are so specific because their platonic idea is so well cemented.</b> When you equate &quot;high place&quot; to lightning, most people don't necessarily equate any high place to lightning. (Although, you could perhaps get more flexible if there is already a storm brewing or active.) You're basically stating &quot;height is a thing that is associated with lightning; ergo, any height will suffice&quot; or more arbitrary yet &quot;this is a building that is sufficiently tall to qualify as a metaphor for lightning; and then using anything defined as a building because a building is higher than the absence of a building ... (aka height acquired?)&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to note that Order and Path tools have actually changed over time. <br /> <br /> This interesting little tidbit and its implications were raised in The Sundered World and To The Strongest chapters in Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, this and other Yantra issues will be expounded upon even further (such as further examples of how Prime might interact with Yantras) in Signs of Sorcery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:31:42-08:00","id":1048124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048123#post1048123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just want to note that Order and Path tools have actually changed over time.<br /> <br /> This interesting little tidbit and its implications were raised in The Sundered World and To The Strongest chapters in Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, this and other Yantra issues will be expounded upon even further (such as further examples of how Prime might interact with Yantras) in Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did they change to/from other widely recognized instruments, though?<br /> <br /> More specifically, did those different tools have widely accepted definitions/attributes or platonic associations? Like going from &quot;gardening hoe&quot; to &quot;knife&quot;? Or was it a more nuanced move. Like moving from a tool that <i>was</i> very well recognized and meaningful in the era, but not so much as time went on and kingdoms fell/rose.<br /> <br /> If so, then the importance of significance carries over, but I've walked away with more knowledge; so thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I thought tools were more or less statically declared for Orders and Paths.<br /> <br /> The more ya know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:46:23-08:00","id":1048126,"title":"","content":"I just re-read <b>Werewolf</b> 2E Storytelling section and in one of Ten Commandments ( of RPG ) is '<b><i>Don't Say No</i></b>' - which I stick with Yantra in <b>Mage</b>. If Yantra seems appropriate for spell or player can point Occult Tradition that use this ( like 'Native Americans of New England use this herb for healing' ), I would totally go with that. Also, <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> pointed that you can use various variants of classical Path or Orders Tools made of appropriate materials - like pen instead of wand made of steel for Obrimos or plastic glass instead of cup for Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Yantras mentioned in corebook are just 'true and tested' - Path, Order or Legacies Tool will work always - everything more should be talked for between players and ST. But generally, i think that 'Rule of Cool' should works in using Yantras, simply to make magic more... well, magical. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2017, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:02:11-08:00","id":1048129,"title":"","content":"That's because wands are not literally wands, they are objects used to point at something or single something out. Pen ascended to this probably because tons of people point at something using their pen, or mark a SINGLE WORD with a circle, and so on. A laser pointer is both a Wand and a Complex Device for purposes of Yantras, for example.<br /> When asking yourself if something is a Yantra, here is a handy procedure:<br /> <br /> 1. Can I map the object to the symbolism and functionality of the Cups, Wands, Mirrors, Swords and Coins? <br /> 1a) If no...Can I map the object to the symbolism of my Order?<br /> 2. Is it made of appropriate material that resonates with my Path?<br /> 3. Is the object symbolically linked to the spell? If no, can I USE IT (as in, physically, ritually use) in a way that clicks with the symbolism of the spell?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:21:38-08:00","id":1048134,"title":"","content":"Design in the book, in general, allows every object to potentially be a yantra (it's extremely hard to find something that doesn't map to the Cups/Wands/Mirrors/Swords/Coins set), while also making the process not meaningless like it would be if it was so open ended that you ccould literally reach to the nearest trash can and grab a set of yantras out of it 10 times out of 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:40:31-08:00","id":1048385,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of Sacraments and Environmental Yantras, but what about Sacraments that you can't claim and keep but you also can't destroy?<br /> \u200bFor example the first light on the first day of the Chinese New Year, or shaking hands when casting binding Fate spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:48:34-08:00","id":1048387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048385#post1048385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the idea of Sacraments and Environmental Yantras, but what about Sacraments that you can't claim and keep but you also can't destroy?<br /> \u200bFor example the first light on the first day of the Chinese New Year, or shaking hands when casting binding Fate spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>First example is an Environmental Yantra, second example isn't a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:05:05-08:00","id":1048397,"title":"","content":"It can be a Yantra if your Persona is one of a magical businessman, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:51:54-08:00","id":1048410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048397#post1048397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be a Yantra if your Persona is one of a magical businessman, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you actually spend the XP purchase the appropriate Shadow Name and the spell has a semiotic link (although in your example, the handshake would likely only be a viable Yantra for a Personna of a powerful businessman for Fate spells dealing with material gain or control, not something as general as all agreements). <br /> <br /> However, none of the standard Yantra categories will allow a simple handshake to provide a Yantra bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:01:08-08:00","id":1048414,"title":"","content":"2ptTakrill didn't limit it to 'a simple handshake.' Handshakes have a lot of symbolism and a lot of meaning, to the point that there are secret handshakes and secret signals sent by handshakes. It's entirely within the bounds of the game for a handshake to be a Mudra, for instance with a Socialize, Persuasion, or even Occult or Politics Skill.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.whale.to/b/masoni62.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But yes. A 'simple handshake' completely disassociated from anything else wouldn't offer a Yantra bonus, but all things go that way if you take away all meaning to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:19:25-08:00","id":1048418,"title":"","content":"I can see the New Year example being treated as Environmental as long as we accept moments in time as environments, not just places and conditions, I could even see a handshake being treated as a Mudra or even coin (Coins are after all only a symbol of trade, even Roman coins were only significant because stamping was the Empire's promise that it contained the claimed amount of pure silver) but that really wasn't the point of the question.<br /> \u200bWhat I was trying to ask is what about symbolic 'things' that can't be kept for later use but also can't be physically destroyed, where would you draw the line between Sacraments and just Fallen World symbols that somehow don't hold Supernal truth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:30:57-08:00","id":1048421,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a> the third word of the Environment Yantra description is &quot;times.&quot; So obviously, an accurate reading says that a time can be an environment for the purpose of casting.<br /> <br /> Fallen World symbols that don't hold Supernal truth wouldn't be Yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T15:40:29-08:00","id":1048451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048414#post1048414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2ptTakrill didn't limit it to 'a simple handshake.' Handshakes have a lot of symbolism and a lot of meaning, to the point that there are secret handshakes and secret signals sent by handshakes. It's entirely within the bounds of the game for a handshake to be a Mudra, for instance with a Socialize, Persuasion, or even Occult or Politics Skill.<br /> <br /> But yes. A 'simple handshake' completely disassociated from anything else wouldn't offer a Yantra bonus, but all things go that way if you take away all meaning to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A mundra is only a Yantra as part of a specific Rote. If you have a Rote of a spell, with a skill specialization in something like Socialize or Persuasion, a handshake can certainly be an expression of the rote skill used to receive the Mundra bonus as part of the Rote.<br /> <br /> However, a handshake, no matter how semiotically connected to a spell, would not provide a Yantra by itself without additional merits or a legacy connection.<br /> <br /> Only the delineated acts provide Yantra bonuses (e.g., concentration, High Speech,<i> Rote</i> Mundras, runes, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T20:25:06-08:00","id":1048560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048421#post1048421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fallen World symbols that don't hold Supernal truth wouldn't be Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallen World symbols would have to be tainted or consumed by the Abyss for them notto hold any Supernal Truth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T01:21:29-08:00","id":1048624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048560#post1048560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fallen World symbols would have to be tainted or consumed by the Abyss for them notto hold any Supernal Truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was answering the question in the words given, and it doesn't change the fact that some symbols in the Fallen world don't have enough sympathy to the Supernal to function as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:35:49-08:00","id":1048942,"title":"","content":"The question really has nothing to do with a handshake, that was just an attempt at an example, the question was about using things that can only be used once but can't physically be destroyed as a Sacrament.<br /> \u200bThe idea is to come up with interesting Yantra that can't be found at the local hardware store, something the acquisition of can be a quest of its own. Given the limits of available Yantra by Path, Order and Legacy I was hoping to reclaim some of the feel of seeking out rare and unusual components in the name of casting a spell, most likely ritual, the effects of which would normally be beyond the Mage's baseline ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:46:56-08:00","id":1048946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048942#post1048942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe idea is to come up with interesting Yantra that can't be found at the local hardware store, something the acquisition of can be a quest of its own. Given the limits of available Yantra by Path, Order and Legacy I was hoping to reclaim some of the feel of seeking out rare and unusual components in the name of casting a spell, most likely ritual, the effects of which would normally be beyond the Mage's baseline ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Sacraments are for, but you have to be able to destroy them or they don't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:59:42-08:00","id":1048951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1048942#post1048942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question really has nothing to do with a handshake, that was just an attempt at an example, the question was about using things that can only be used once but can't physically be destroyed as a Sacrament.<br /> \u200bThe idea is to come up with interesting Yantra that can't be found at the local hardware store, something the acquisition of can be a quest of its own. Given the limits of available Yantra by Path, Order and Legacy I was hoping to reclaim some of the feel of seeking out rare and unusual components in the name of casting a spell, most likely ritual, the effects of which would normally be beyond the Mage's baseline ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might be interested in reading about Quintessences in Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <br /> They're basically unique Sacraments necessary to cast Imperial spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:47:46-08:00","id":1049077,"title":"","content":"I've debated buying Imperial Mysteries but my chronicles aren't of the world shaking variety and everything I've read about it indicates it is. Am I wrong?<br /> \u200bWhat I really want from the Yantra rules and they aren't providing according to the book, is a good reason why my characters, when casting a powerful ward around their sanctum, would go through the trouble of retrieving a stone from the Great Wall of China instead of just buying a fence post from Home Depot (that is just an example). Plus 2 reach just doesn't really feel worth it, not when Home Depot can also sale me a few feet of barb wire and a no trespassing sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 02-14-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T19:24:17-08:00","id":1049095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047834-yantra-limitations?p=1049077#post1049077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWhat I really want from the Yantra rules and they aren't providing according to the book, is a good reason why my characters, when casting a powerful ward around their sanctum, would go through the trouble of retrieving a stone from the Great Wall of China instead of just buying a fence post from Home Depot (that is just an example). Plus 2 reach just doesn't really feel worth it, not when Home Depot can also sale me a few feet of barb wire and a no trespassing sign.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Home Depot doesn't sell anti-teleport locks and two dice is the difference between year-long wards and functionally-permanent wards, or wards that cover a single floor and wards that cover a small building, or wards whose backdoors have one layer of security and wards whose backdoors have two layers of security.<br /> <br /> A +2 Yantra is valuable because it saves you a Yantra slot, not because the extra +1 is inherently valuable on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}